--TEST--
A `static`, variadic or `inout` member of a delegated interface is refused where the clause is written, and an own method answers it instead — `rule:classes/delegation-by-field`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:classes/delegation-by-field`'s forward is a whole synthesized method whose body passes its
// parameters straight on, so three member shapes have no forward: a `static`
// member has no receiver to read the field off, and a variadic or `inout`
// parameter list is packed and written back at the *call site*, so passing it
// on would do that twice.
//
// Each used to be silent — no forward, no obligation, and a call landing on
// `nvs_runtime::nvs_abstract_method`, a FATAL naming a compiler bug for a
// program the front end had accepted. They are `E0721` where the clause is
// written now, sorted by member name, so a shape that stops refusing shows up
// as a missing line rather than as a crash a milestone later.
interface Wide {
    public static function make(): string;
    public function join(string ...$parts): string;
    public function bump(inout int $n): void;
    public function plain(): string;
}

// All three refused; `plain` is forwarded and says nothing.
final class Holder implements Wide by $inner {
    private Wide $inner;
    public function constructor(Wide $inner) { $this->inner = $inner; }
}

// The way out the help names: an own method stands in for a delegated one,
// which § 4 already allows — so `Written` owes only the two it did not write.
final class Written implements Wide by $inner {
    private Wide $inner;
    public function constructor(Wide $inner) { $this->inner = $inner; }
    public static function make(): string { return "made"; }
    public function bump(inout int $n): void { $n = $n + 1; }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0721]: `Wide::bump` cannot be forwarded to `$inner`, so `Holder` has to declare it
%A
error[E0721]: `Wide::join` cannot be forwarded to `$inner`, so `Holder` has to declare it
%A
error[E0721]: `Wide::make` cannot be forwarded to `$inner`, so `Holder` has to declare it
%A
error[E0721]: `Wide::join` cannot be forwarded to `$inner`, so `Written` has to declare it
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
